  "whichCorner": "Which corner are you aiming at?",
  "whichCornerBody": "From where you are now, aim at the foot of a corner you already marked. That tells the app where you are again and the plan stays put.",
  "legacyHelpBody": "1. Tap «Not calibrated» and type the ceiling height. Aim at the foot of a wall, lock it, then at the ceiling of that same wall. That tells the app how high you are holding the phone so it measures properly.\n2. Put the crosshair at the foot of a corner, where the wall meets the floor, and mark it.\n3. Turn on the spot: a line runs from the marked corner and follows the crosshair. Mark the next one and the wall is made.\n4. When you come back to the first corner the line snaps to it: that closes the room.\n\nIf you have to walk, tap «I moved», aim at a corner you already marked and fix your position: the plan stays where it is.\n\nAll of this is an estimate: afterwards you can correct each wall with a tape measure in the plan editor.",
